1
00:00:00,145 --> 00:00:01,558
He fainted on
the stairs.

2
00:00:01,855 --> 00:00:04,137
That single detail
decides the question.

3
00:00:04,788 --> 00:00:07,386
A 74-year-old man
comes to the clinic

4
00:00:07,406 --> 00:00:09,584
because of a 6-month
history of shortness

5
00:00:09,604 --> 00:00:10,925
of breath with
exertion.

6
00:00:11,156 --> 00:00:13,150
Last week he lost
consciousness while

7
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:15,229
climbing the stairs
to his apartment and

8
00:00:15,249 --> 00:00:16,741
recovered within
a minute.

9
00:00:16,972 --> 00:00:18,320
He has no chest pain.

10
00:00:18,551 --> 00:00:24,175
Blood pressure 128/76
mmHg, pulse 72/min.

11
00:00:24,472 --> 00:00:26,977
Cardiac examination
shows a harsh,

12
00:00:27,025 --> 00:00:29,136
crescendo-decrescendo
systolic murmur

13
00:00:29,156 --> 00:00:31,202
loudest at the right
second intercostal

14
00:00:31,222 --> 00:00:34,254
space, radiating to
both carotid arteries.

15
00:00:34,485 --> 00:00:36,451
The second heart
sound is soft.

16
00:00:36,683 --> 00:00:39,018
The carotid upstroke
is delayed and low

17
00:00:39,038 --> 00:00:41,400
in amplitude. The
lungs are clear and

18
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,149
there is no
peripheral edema.

19
00:00:45,156 --> 00:00:46,859
Pause. Pick
your answer.

20
00:00:50,361 --> 00:00:51,814
The answer is A.

21
00:00:52,006 --> 00:00:54,065
Fixed stroke volume
limiting the rise in

22
00:00:54,085 --> 00:00:56,195
cardiac output
during exertion.

23
00:00:56,841 --> 00:00:59,163
A stenotic valve
cannot open wider when

24
00:00:59,183 --> 00:01:01,847
demand rises. At rest
the stiff ventricle

25
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:04,071
still generates
adequate output; on

26
00:01:04,091 --> 00:01:07,097
exertion stroke volume
is capped, cardiac

27
00:01:07,117 --> 00:01:09,374
output fails to
rise, and cerebral

28
00:01:09,394 --> 00:01:10,517
perfusion falls.

29
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:15,036
Exertional syncope
is a haemodynamic

30
00:01:15,056 --> 00:01:17,839
problem until proven
otherwise: the heart

31
00:01:17,859 --> 00:01:20,969
cannot meet demand.
Aortic stenosis,

32
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:23,720
hypertrophic cardiomyopathy
and pulmonary

33
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:25,851
hypertension are
the three causes.

34
00:01:27,843 --> 00:01:30,086
The full breakdown,
with all four wrong

35
00:01:30,106 --> 00:01:32,244
answers and what
would have made each

36
00:01:32,264 --> 00:01:34,190
one correct, is
on the channel.
